//   issue:      flat name of the Cheng issue fn (called by the await-split seg0 with the real args)
//   injectArgs: a fn(rc) -> the route-content-derived send-arg free-vars to inject so the inner-fn
//               send call (`<callee>(content.id, <argN>)`) resolves to REAL sources. `rc` is the
//               handler's single-route content ({id, isLiked}); content.id is always available, the
//               other args come from already-injected state slots (e.g. commentText) or the route.
// Adding a service is mechanical: append a row. Route-content resolution stays per-handler (below).
// `content` (struct {id}) is the shared first-arg source — injected once via injectContentArg.
